ressbook><name>TAKAGAHARA ISAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMURA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAGUCHI, KICHITARO DI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>LEE, Y., C.</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATUO, YUHSI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, KEIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGAHARA, ISAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMURA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A novel method for assaying C-reactive protein (CRP) in a sample whereby the concentration of CRP in the sample is assayed by utilizing the specific binding of phosphocholine (PC) to CRP. More particularly, a novel method for assaying CRP concentration in a sample characterized in that, in the sandwich method, CRP in the sample bonded to a solid phase is detected by using PC labeled with a radioactive isotope, a fluorochrome (fluorescein, lanthanoid), etc. By using this method, serum CRP concentration at a noraml level can be accurately determined.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Nouvelle méthode de dosage de protéine C-réactive (CRP) dans un échantillon par laquelle la concentration de CRP dans l'échantillon est dosée à l'aide de la liaison spécifique de la phosphocholine (PC) à la CRP. Plus particulièrement, l'invention a trait à une nouvelle méthode de dosage de la concentration de CRP dans un échantillon caractérisée en ce que, dans la méthode en sandwich, la CRP dans l'échantillon liée à une phase solide est détectée à l'aide de PC marquée par un isotope radioactif, un fluorochrome (fluorescéine, lanthanoïde), etc. L'utilisation de cette méthode permet de déterminer avec précision la concentration de CRP dans le sérum à un niveau normal.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>